s banner never gained hand-tan  combat training and is often portrayed  as a little timid sure he impressively  defeated kul obsidian during avengers  infinity war but that fight would not  have lasted very long without tony  stark's hulkbuster outfit keeping things  equal jennifer walters is not a highly  trained combatant she's a successful  lawyer dedicated to her career still  she's much more confident than her meek  scientist cousin based on the  relationship showcased in she-hulk's  attorney of law we suspect that walters  regularly came out on top during  childhood familial roughhousing and if  the two were to fight without their  hulking abilities there's reason to  believe that walters would take the win  if the influx of superhero shows and  movies has proven anything it's that you  need someone on your super team who  packs a mighty punch in the comics a  version of the hulk has often been part  of the avengers lineup in fact he was  part of the very first lineup however  deciding who to recruit becomes  difficult when choosing between a raging  giant beast and a composed powerhouse in  the case of hulk he's as strong as they  come and can take on some of the biggest  challenges unfortunately his penchant  for flying off the handle and causing  more destruction than good can become  more of a burden than anything else  conversely she-hulk is a woman who keeps  her composure most of the time at least  and she can deliver blows of near equal  strength to her powerful cousin plus  jennifer walters has the added bonus of  being an established lawyer while it's  always nice to have a physicist around  having someone who can take care of  legal business in your squad certainly  sounds more promising  both hulk and she-hulk have been part of  the marvel collection for decades  she-hulk first appeared in 1980 with her  self-titled comic book her relation to  bruce banner helped her quickly befriend  many superheroes and she soon became a  member of teams like the